<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm on poor arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm on poor arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices firmed on poor arrivals against good demand from processing plants on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices were up by 100 to 150 rupees per tonne in central Indian Markets.</p>
<p>Dealers said soybean yellow was in the price range of 10,100-10,500 rupees in the markets and 10,250-10,650 rupees in plant delivery condition.</p>
<p>Markets in central India will be closed on Thursday due to a local religious holiday.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on good export demand against poor selling. Soymeal yellow was $278 to $279 per tonne in export FAS (free alongside ship) Bedibunder. Rapeseed extraction was $131 to $132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,525 rupees for Bedibunder and was 4,500 rupees for Bhavnager. The undertone was strong.</p>
